From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Turcios <turcioskevinr@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:30:54 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Face Swap: video delay to keep lips in sync with realtime
 voice

Vendored Deep-Live-Cam: DelayedSink wraps a frame sink and forwards each
frame delay_ms later (adjustable while running; lowering it skips ahead
instead of bursting a backlog; 0 passes straight through).

Face Swap tab: "Video delay (ms)" slider wraps the virtual-camera output
(the preview stays undelayed) and applies live. "Match voice delay"
estimates it from the Realtime tab's chunk and crossfade settings
(voice ~ chunk + crossfade + 25 ms, minus ~65 ms of video lag; 260 ms
with the defaults), and "Start face + voice" applies that estimate when
the delay is 0. The Realtime tab exposes its chunk/crossfade controls in
SESSION_CONTROLS for this.

Applio-Commit: 84a4b38be96edcb2c80c4bf0f19ee3fa2185c8ca
